# License

This repository holds two kinds of material under different terms: work
authored here, and third-party content vendored from upstream. Rather than
apply one blanket license — which would misrepresent the vendored material —
this file grants terms over the authored work in **Part 1** and records the
vendored content in **Part 2**.

Read Part 2 before copying anything out of `collections/`.

---

## Part 1 — Grant for authored work

**Copyright © 2026 Sanjeev Kumar**

Permission is granted to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute,
sublicense, and/or sell copies of the authored work, and to permit others to
do so, subject to:

1. **Attribution.** This license and the copyright notice above must accompany
   any copy or substantial portion of the authored work.
2. **Derived works.** Modified versions must state that they were modified, and
   must not claim endorsement by the author.
3. **No warranty.** The work is provided as-is, without warranty of any kind,
   express or implied.
4. **Limitation of liability.** The author is not liable for any claim or
   damages arising from the work or its use.

### Scope: what the authored work covers

Everything in this repository **except**:

- the third-party collections enumerated in Part 2, and
- any path carrying its own `LICENSE`, `LICENCE`, `COPYING`, or `NOTICE` file —
  those files govern their own directory.

Authored work includes `scripts/`, `tests/`, `benchmarks/`, `canonical/`,
`skills/`, and the first-party collections `agentic-design-patterns/`,
`claude-agent-architectures/`, `enterprise-ops/`, and
`reference-architectures/`.

### Paths carrying their own license

Those files govern their directories; this license does not apply to them.
Notably `skills/attention-span/`, which is **AGPL-3.0** — copyleft, and cannot
be relicensed under the terms above by anyone who has already received it.

---

## Part 2 — Vendored third-party content

`collections/` is synced from upstream projects. Each vendored tree retains its
own `LICENSE` where one was supplied, and **none of it is covered by Part 1**.

| Collection | Upstream | Terms |
|---|---|---|
| `academic-research-skills/` | `github.com/Imbad0202/academic-research-skills` | **CC BY-NC 4.0** © 2026 Cheng-I Wu — non-commercial, incompatible with a permissive grant |
| `cybersecurity-skills/` | `github.com/mukul975/Anthropic-Cybersecurity-Skills` | Apache-2.0 |
| `ecc-upstream/` | `github.com/apps/ecc-tools` | MIT |
| `financial-services/` | `github.com/anthropics/financial-services` | Apache-2.0 |
| `huggingface-skills/` | `github.com/huggingface/skills` | Apache-2.0 |
| `impeccable/` | `github.com/anthropics/skills` | Apache-2.0 |
| `kaggle-skills/` | Kaggle (official) | Apache-2.0 |
| `open-code-review/` | `github.com/alibaba/open-code-review` | Apache-2.0 |
| `media-production/` | mixed sources | no top-level license; `diagrams/` ships MIT |
| `scientific-skills/` | mixed sources | no top-level license; most content Apache-2.0, `pacsomatic/` MIT |

Where a collection ships no single top-level license, its per-subdirectory
`LICENSE` files govern the corresponding subdirectories.

---

## Part 3 — Dependencies and contributions

**Dependencies are not vendored.** Node packages are installed from each
project's `package-lock.json` via `npm ci`; `node_modules/` is git-ignored.
Each dependency retains its own upstream license.

**Contributions** to the authored work are accepted under Part 1. The
third-party collections in Part 2 are synced from upstream and do not accept
local edits — they will be overwritten on the next sync.